Package: kelixip-mod-presence
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.ives.fr/
Depends: kelixip (= @VERSION@)
Description: Presence collection module for kelixip
 The presence collection (RFC 3856 / RFC 3903): the published state of each
 presentity with its entity-tag, the live subscriptions to it, and the fan-out
 that turns one PUBLISH into one NOTIFY per watcher. Its records are kamailio's
 presentity and active_watchers rows, held in memory. Enable it with a
 [module.presence] block in config.toml, and declare the packages a domain
 serves with [[domain.presence]] blocks in domains.toml.
 .
 Who may watch whom is NOT decided here: the reference scripts are, and that is
 where a deployment writes its rule.
 .
 The payload is BEAM bytecode, but the package is architecture-dependent on
 purpose: it must be built and shipped alongside the core whose embedded ERTS
 will load it.
